name loc-feed
# The Library of Congress's Atom feed of changes to ISO 639-5. The feed is a page about the list, not the list: its
# entries (title, id, updated, published, author, category, link, and the change described in each entry's content)
# say when and where the Library of Congress published a change, and attest nothing of a language. The feed is read
# as content of the file, in its tree, and makes no claim (Laplace-Engine#32: "the feed is the file's metadata or a
# page: it attests nothing about languages; read it as content of the file"). The changes themselves are the list's,
# which loc.recipe reads from iso639-5.rdf.
match iso639-5.atom10.xml
witness Library of Congress
format xml

thing feed id
thing entry id
omit xmlns xmlns:* xml:lang length
content *
